Files included:
- SmtpProxy.java   (source code)
- SmtpProxy.class  (executable)
- README.txt       (this file)

How to run the proxy:
1. Ensure Java is installed (see commands below).
2. Start your SMTP server (e.g., the provided MockSmtpServer) on port 8025.
3. Compile: javac SmtpProxy.java
4. Run: java SmtpProxy
5. Connect a client (e.g., telnet) to localhost:55555.

Extra features implemented:
- Logging of all email modifications to proxy.log (audit trail)
- Statistics (total emails, Illuminati replacements, word substitutions)
- Multi‑threaded client handling
- Multi‑word and case‑insensitive substitutions (e.g., "very good" → "plusgood")
- Illuminati detection (replaces whole email with "Hello world")

